### Configure the Ubuntu Server
- On Oracle VM Box, select the Virtual Machine as 'Bridge'.
- Download the Ubuntu Server ISO from the official Ubuntu site.
- Configure on a Virtual Box Machine as:
  - Your Name: UbuntuLab
  - Your Server Name: Wazuh
  - Pick a Server Username: wazuhadm  
  https://github.com/AbnerStier/Wazuh-Lab/blob/main/images/ubuntu-wazuhconfig.png?raw=true

- Install Wazuh on Ubuntu Server using the script:
  curl -sO https://packages.wazuh.com/4.14/wazuh-install.sh && sudo bash ./wazuh-install.sh -a

### Or use a pre-made Virtual Machine box in the 'Wazuh Installation Alternatives' section.
  https://github.com/AbnerStier/Wazuh-Lab/blob/main/images/wazuh-OVA.png

### After the installation type 'ip -a' to get the Wazuh IP to access the dashboard
  https://github.com/AbnerStier/Wazuh-Lab/blob/main/images/wazuh-ip-a.png

---

### Deploy an Agent
#### After accessing the Dashboard we will need to deploy the agent on the Windows AD Server
- Navigate to the 'Agents Summary' -> 'Deploy New Agent' -> 'Assign Server Address'. It will be the same as Wazuh.
- Assign an Agent Name: Windows-AD

- Go to the Windows Server -> Open PowerShell as Administrator -> Run the command:
  Invoke-WebRequest -Uri https://packages.wazuh.com/4.x/windows/wazuh-agent-4.14.5-1.msi -OutFile $env:tmp\wazuh-agent; msiexec.exe /i $env:tmp\wazuh-agent /q WAZUH_MANAGER='(the IP of the Wazuh Server Address)' WAZUH_AGENT_GROUP='default' WAZUH_AGENT_NAME='Windows-AD'

- Finish with:
  NET START Wazuh
